# Without an HPET, and without Hyper-V's reference counter, the kernel has
# nothing to calibrate the local APIC timer against and panics rather than
# guess a rate (docs/design.md, "The timer"). Up to that point it boots:
# the ACPI summary says there is no HPET and the rest is unchanged.
cmdline: test=hello
qemu_args: -machine hpet=off
exit: failure
expect: acpi: MADT flags 0x1 PCAT_COMPAT
expect: acpi: COM1 is ISA IRQ 4 -> GSI 4, edge, active high
expect: acpi: no HPET
expect: acpi: ECAM segment 0, buses 0-255, at 0xe0000000
expect: hyperv: no TLFS interface
expect: apic: xAPIC ID 0
expect: ioapic: 0:
expect: KERNEL PANIC at kernel/src/arch/x86_64/timer.rs:
expect: no timer reference
